<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.50%" pitch="-2.50%">
      Jacob began to prepare.<break time="500ms"/>
      He divided his people into two camps.<break time="500ms"/>
      If Esau attacks one, he thought, perhaps the other may escape.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Then Jacob prayed.<break time="500ms"/>
      He said, O God of my father Abraham, God of my father Isaac.<break time="500ms"/>
      You told me to return, and you said you would do me good.<break time="1000ms"/>
      I am not worthy of the least of all the steadfast love you have shown your servant.<break time="1800ms"/>

      With only my staff I crossed this Jordan.<break time="500ms"/>
      And now I have become two camps.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Please deliver me from the hand of my brother.<break time="1800ms"/>

      It was an honest prayer.<break time="500ms"/>
      The prayer of a man who knew he had done wrong and could not undo it.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Then Jacob chose gifts from his flocks.<break time="500ms"/>
      Two hundred female goats and twenty male goats.<break time="500ms"/>
      Two hundred ewes and twenty rams.<break time="500ms"/>
      Thirty milking camels with their young.<break time="500ms"/>
      Forty cows and ten bulls.<break time="500ms"/>
      Twenty female donkeys and ten male donkeys.<break time="1800ms"/>

      He sent them ahead in waves, one drove after another.<break time="500ms"/>
      Each servant carried the same message for Esau.<break time="500ms"/>
      They belong to your servant Jacob. They are a gift sent to my lord Esau.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Then Jacob sent his wives and children across the brook Jabbok.<break time="500ms"/>
      Everything he had, he sent across.<break time="1000ms"/>
      And Jacob was left alone.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Sometimes you must send everything ahead and stand with nothing.<break time="1000ms"/>
      You can rest.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
